  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Quest can't handle as many PhysBones as PC, so PhysBones often need to be deleted when porting a PC avatar to Quest.\n\nDeleting PhysBones can desync them between PC and Quest. But the documentation doesn't mention that, and doesn't clarify how to avoid it.\n\n---\n\nhere's how PhysBone sync works:\n- VRChat fully expands your Unity Hierarchy\n- then it goes through every GameObject one-by-one, top-to-bottom\n- when it encounters a PhysBone, it internally gives that PhysBone an ID number, starting from 0 and counting up. (it's impossible to see this number)\n\nif there's 1 PC-only bone above the cross-platform bones, the ID numbers will be off by 1. if there's 2 PC-only bones above the cross-platform bones, the ID numbers will be off by 2. and so on.\n\nyou need to make sure that these ID numbers are the same on both platforms. you do this by drag-and-dropping objects in the Hierarchy. all the cross-platform PhysBones need to be above the PC-only PhysBones. \n\nif you can't make this happen by dragging Armature GameObjects, you can copy and paste PhysBone components onto empty GameObjects, and drag those.\n\n---\n\ngiven that PhysBones frequently need to be deleted for Quest compatibility, this should be noted in the PhysBones documentation.",
